{"type": "text", "text": "I have everything needed. Here is the complete report.

# JIT Context Feature — Codebase Findings

Note: the repo root is `/workspace/repo` (not `/workspace`). All paths below are absolute.

---

## 1. `Config` class — `/workspace/repo/packages/core/src/config/config.ts`

**Class definition** (line 635):
```ts
export class Config implements McpContext, AgentLoopContext {
```
Constructor at line 844 (`constructor(params: ConfigParameters)`); the `ConfigParameters` interface is at line 503.

Relevant private fields:
- Line 613 (in `ConfigParameters`): `experimentalJitContext?: boolean;`
- Line 830: `private readonly experimentalJitContext: boolean;`
- Line 836: `private contextManager?: ContextManager;`
- Line 931 (constructor): `this.experimentalJitContext = params.experimentalJitContext ?? false;`
- Import at line 106: `import { ContextManager } from '../services/contextManager.js';`

The `ContextManager` is instantiated lazily (lines 1237-1239):
```ts
if (this.experimentalJitContext) {
  this.contextManager = new ContextManager(this);
  await this.contextManager.refresh();
}
```

**All three requested methods exist.**

`getContextManager()` and `isJitContextEnabled()` (lines 1988-1994):
```ts
getContextManager(): ContextManager | undefined {
  return this.contextManager;
}

isJitContextEnabled(): boolean {
  return this.experimentalJitContext;
}
```

`getWorkspaceContext()` (lines 1677-1679):
```ts
getWorkspaceContext(): WorkspaceContext {
  return this.workspaceContext;
}
```

Related surrounding methods that already integrate the ContextManager:
- `getGlobalMemory()` (1980) → `this.contextManager?.getGlobalMemory() ?? ''`
- `getEnvironmentMemory()` (1984) → `this.contextManager?.getEnvironmentMemory() ?? ''`
- `getUserMemory()` (1947-1956) — returns a `HierarchicalMemory` object from the contextManager when JIT is on, else `this.userMemory`:
```ts
getUserMemory(): string | HierarchicalMemory {
  if (this.experimentalJitContext && this.contextManager) {
    return {
      global: this.contextManager.getGlobalMemory(),
      extension: this.contextManager.getExtensionMemory(),
      project: this.contextManager.getEnvironmentMemory(),
    };
  }
  return this.userMemory;
}
```
- `refreshMcpContext()` (1961-) calls `this.contextManager.refresh()` when JIT is enabled.

---

## 2. `ContextManager` — `/workspace/repo/packages/core/src/services/contextManager.ts`

Class declared at line 21 (`export class ContextManager`). Full class is 188 lines; key parts:

Fields + constructor (lines 22-31):
```ts
private readonly loadedPaths: Set<string> = new Set();
private readonly loadedFileIdentities: Set<string> = new Set();
private readonly config: Config;
private globalMemory: string = '';
private extensionMemory: string = '';
private projectMemory: string = '';

constructor(config: Config) {
  this.config = config;
}
```

`refresh()` (lines 36-45):
```ts
async refresh(): Promise<void> {
  this.loadedPaths.clear();
  this.loadedFileIdentities.clear();

  const paths = await this.discoverMemoryPaths();
  const contentsMap = await this.loadMemoryContents(paths);

  this.categorizeMemoryContents(paths, contentsMap);
  this.emitMemoryChanged();
}
```

`discoverContext()` — signature and body (lines 129-160). This is the JIT/Tier-3 hook, and note it currently has **no callers** anywhere in the repo (only defined here) — it is the integration point the feature needs to wire up:
```ts
async discoverContext(
  accessedPath: string,
  trustedRoots: string[],
): Promise<string> {
  if (!this.config.isTrustedFolder()) {
    return '';
  }
  const result = await loadJitSubdirectoryMemory(
    accessedPath,
    trustedRoots,
    this.loadedPaths,
    this.loadedFileIdentities,
  );

  if (result.files.length === 0) {
    return '';
  }

  const newFilePaths = result.files.map((f) => f.path);
  this.markAsLoaded(newFilePaths);

  if (result.fileIdentities) {
    for (const identity of result.fileIdentities) {
      this.loadedFileIdentities.add(identity);
    }
  }
  return concatenateInstructions(
    result.files.map((f) => ({ filePath: f.path, content: f.content })),
    this.config.getWorkingDir(),
  );
}
```

Other public getters: `getGlobalMemory()` (168), `getExtensionMemory()` (172), `getEnvironmentMemory()` (176), `getLoadedPaths(): ReadonlySet<string>` (184). It emits `CoreEvent.MemoryChanged` via `emitMemoryChanged()` (162).

`discoverContext` relies on `loadJitSubdirectoryMemory` and `concatenateInstructions` imported from `../utils/memoryDiscovery.js` (lines 7-17).

---

## 3. `getWorkspaceContext` / `WorkspaceContext` — `/workspace/repo/packages/core/src/utils/workspaceContext.ts`

Class at line 24 (`export class WorkspaceContext`). `getDirectories()` (lines 153-155):
```ts
getDirectories(): readonly string[] {
  return Array.from(this.directories);
}
```
Related: `getInitialDirectories(): readonly string[]` (157), `setDirectories(directories: readonly string[]): void` (161).

`Config.getWorkspaceContext()` returns this instance (config.ts:1677, see item 1). The ContextManager already uses `this.config.getWorkspaceContext().getDirectories()` (contextManager.ts:55) to build trusted roots for memory discovery.

---

## 4. `resetChat` — `/workspace/repo/packages/core/src/core/client.ts`

Defined on the client class (lines 299-302):
```ts
async resetChat(): Promise<void> {
  this.chat = await this.startChat();
  this.updateTelemetryTokenCount();
}
```

Surrounding context: `dispose()` (304), `resumeChat()` (308), `addDirectoryContext()` (328), `updateSystemInstruction()` (339-347) — which calls `getCoreSystemPrompt(this.config, this.config.getUserMemory())` — and `startChat()` (349). Relevant imports at top of file: `getCoreSystemPrompt` from `./prompts.js` (line 29), `getDirectoryContextString` / `getInitialChatHistory` from `../utils/environmentContext.js` (17-18), and `type Config` from `../config/config.js` (27).

Callers of `resetChat()`: client.ts lines 946 & 964 (internal), and `/workspace/repo/packages/cli/src/ui/commands/clearCommand.ts:48` (`await geminiClient.resetChat();`).

---

## 5. Tool `execute` methods and `llmContent` construction

All under `/workspace/repo/packages/core/src/tools/`. Each returns a `ToolResult` with `llmContent` (string or `PartUnion`/`PartListUnion`) + `returnDisplay`.

### edit.ts — `EditTool` invocation (`execute` at line 824)
Success path builds a joined string message array (lines 915-943):
```ts
